# Private Workspace Repo — Private Agent Rules (Example)

Copy to `AGENTS.md` at the root of your **private workspace repo** (a
separate, private repository — not part of this template repo, and not a
container for project repos). This is the file agents read first whenever
the private workspace is available, in addition to (never instead of)
whichever single project repo's own public `AGENTS.md` applies to the
current task.

Consolidates categories 1 and 2 from `private/README.md`: Local Environment
& Credentials, and Cross-Service Relationships & Change Patterns. Team Mode
Agent Design and Workflow Rules stay in their own files
(`team-mode-design.local.md`, `workflow-rules.local.md`) and are referenced
from here.

## Required First Steps for Agents Using This Private Workspace

1. Read this file when the private workspace is available.
2. Read `team-mode-design.local.md` for team structure and role mapping.
3. Read `workflow-rules.local.md` for how to approach work in this org.
4. Confirm which single project repo the task concerns, then read that
   project's own `AGENTS.md` (public) before making any change. Never edit
   more than one project repo in the same task.

